# The audioif floor. Every gate in this repository runs against this exact
# audioif commit: the components are held to a fixed core the same way
# audioif itself is held to a fixed CircuitPython (its CIRCUITPYTHON_ORACLE).
#
# A floating core makes a component failure unattributable -- you cannot tell
# a rewritten instrument from a moved node underneath it. Moving this pin is
# its own change, with the gates re-run and the goldens re-read, never a
# side effect of some other work.
#
# From 2026-09-02 this pin named an UNRELEASED commit rather than a release
# tag, deliberately: audioif carried four synthio fixes that the accuracy
# program needed -- the CPython press semantics and filter cascade (b420dac),
# a re-pressed finished note being dropped entirely (afb6b71, also reported
# upstream), ring modulation, which the CPython target had never implemented
# (52a1d4e) and which three Phase 2 instruments depend on, and envelope
# reassignment not being live on the CPython target (d84470a). The release
# waited until the bug hunt settled; the floor did not need to.
#
# Moved to d84470a on 2026-09-02. That fix is what makes one circuit shared by
# two voices with different decays behave correctly under CPython, as it
# already did on MicroPython and the oracle: before it, a closed hat struck
# 250 ms after an open hat rang for 400 ms instead of 53 ms. It changes the
# rendered sound of tr808 and cr78, whose hats share a circuit, so both were
# re-listened.
#
# Moved to v0.2.0 on 2026-09-03, the first audioif release that contains the
# four fixes named above, plus the release-tail reclaim (aed9336) and the
# 14-everywhere Note ceiling (63efb13). The pin names a release again for the
# first time since it moved to d84470a; the floor in each pyproject.toml is
# raised to the same release, so floor and pin agree for the first time as
# well. The tag resolves to the commit in the second column.
#
#
# Moved to 2f6cbc3 on 2026-09-07 by the effects program's Phase 1 (anchor
# docs/effects-roadmap.md; audiocomponents#29). That commit is audioif main
# with the eight palette nodes Phase 0's survey asked for and Phase 1 built
# (audioif#37-#44, #47): four FeedbackDelay options, eleven Dynamics options,
# audioshaper.Waveshaper, audiobiquad.Biquad/AllPass, audioladder.Ladder,
# audioverb.Tank, audiomath.SubOctave and audioroute.MidSide, each with its
# own parity probe and golden, all fifteen probes byte-identical on CPython
# and MicroPython. No release: audioif is released once, at Phase 7, when
# the effects work is complete (Brad, 2026-09-06), so this pin names a commit
# and the pyproject floors stay at v0.2.0 until then. This is also the first
# floor to carry the 64-voice ceiling (audioif 8f8b10d); the three
# instruments the ceiling moves at the gate's material are retired to
# REBUILT with Brad's listen of 2026-09-06 as the blessing (audioif#31).
#
